### Page 7 of 17

```text
exceed $40,000. The Minimum rent payment shall be due on the last day of each month
and percentage rent shall be paid with the minimum rent payment the following month.
4.
Utilities. The Lessee will pay and be responsible for all natural gas and electricity to the
leased premises during the term of this agreement. Lessee shall also pay and be
responsible for City of Cheyenne charges, including but not limited to sewer, water and
dump charges.
5.
Condition of Promises. Lessee covenants that it has, prior to entering into this lease,
inspected the condition of the premises and finds them to be satisfactory in all respects for
the purposes intended. The Lessee agrees to maintain the premises, as well as the
improvements thereon, in as good an order and condition as they were when possession
of said premises was delivered to Lessee, reasonable wear and tear only excepted; and at
the end of the term of this lease, the Lessee will peaceably deliver possession of the
premises to the Lessor in the same or better condition as described above. The premises
are presently in satisfactory condition. Major maintenance of the roof and exterior of the
building and repair or maintenance of heating and plumbing systems shall also be the
responsibility and expense of Lessee.
The Lessee shall not make any alterations or additions in or to the premises
without the prior written consent of Lessor, with the exception of minor repairs and
maintenance as well as day-to-day maintenance on the premises, and in the event
alterations or additions are made which are permanent in nature with the written consent
of Lessor, they shall be and remain a part of the premises upon the termination of this
lease unless otherwise agreed to in writing by Lessor and Lessee.
6.
Use of Premises. The Lessee shall use said premises for the purpose of operation of a
retail liquor establishment or similar or related activity, including, without limitation, the
sale of alcoholic or malt beverages. Lessee shall not permit any unlawful, improper or
offensive use of the premises, nor allow any use or occupancy thereof, which is contrary
to the laws of the State of Wyoming.
7.
Taxes and Assessments. Lessee shall be responsible to timely and directly pay all
property taxes levied upon the leased premises during the term of this Lease Agreement.
In addition, Lessee shall be responsible to pay any and all property assessments levied
Commercial Lease Agreement
Redwood Saloon, LLC.
