### Page 9 of 17

```text
13. Insurance. Lessee agrees to maintain liability insurance coverage for bodily injury or
property damage and content property damage to third parties occurring on the premises.
Liability insurance in the amount of not less than $375,000.00 shall be purchased by
Lessee, having Lessor as an additional Insured. Lessee shall provide Lessor with proof of
insurance. Lessee shall pay the cost of fire and casualty insurance on the property,
insuring the premises and contents according to the parties’ interest.
14. Remedies Upon Default. If the Lessee is in default in the payment of rent or of any of the
other terms hereunder, the Lessor shall give written notice by certified mail or hand
delivery of the default to the Lessee.
If within a 10 day period of the date of the mailing of said notice of default the
Lessee makes the payment and initiates action to cure any other default, then the Lessee’s
right under this lease shall be reinstated and this agreement shall continue to same as if no
default had occurred.
If the Lessee fails or neglects to pay, correct or make good such default as set
forth in said notice of default within 10 days of the date of mailing or delivery of said
notice, then and in that event the Lessor may, at her election, terminate this lease and re
enter into the leased premises either with or without process of law.
The Lessee does
hereby covenant and agree to surrender and deliver up the leased premises peaceably and
immediately upon the termination.
Lessor shall have the right to proceed under any
remedy at law or in equity, including but not limited to the right of forcible entry and
detainer.
In the event of termination for default, Lessee shall be permitted a reasonable
opportunity to remove Lessee’s property from the premises and Lessor shall have no right
of distraint.
15. Miscellaneous.
This agreement shall be deemed to be an integrated agreement,
superseding all prior oral or written agreements between the parties relative to the subject
matter hereof, and shall be binding upon the respective parties, their heirs, successors and
assigns. If any part of this agreement shall be found or held to be invalid, such finding
shall not affect the validity of any other part.
No modification of this agreement or
waiver of any of the terms or conditions hereof shall be of any force and effect unless the
same is in writing, signed by the Lessee and the Lessor.
Time shall be and is of the
Commercial Lease Agreement
